  "query_preview": "..Satellite imagery this morning showed considerable\nmid-high level clouds under southwest flow aloft out ahead of a\nstrong upper level low off southern CA coast. Thunderstorm\nactivity this morning as been across central and northern AZ and\nthat should remain the case through 12 noon. As the upper low\nmoves closer to the SoCal coast, the upper divergent field that\nis NW to Tucson will expand over the area. Scattered showers and\nthunderstorms that develop this afternoon will be capable of\nnear severe strong winds, large hail and brief heavy rain with \nrainfall rates of 1-2\"/hr. This is especially true across Pinal,\nGraham and Greenlee counties. A few strong storms are possible \nthis evening into the overnight hours. For Thursday as the upper\nlevel trof moves inland there will be another round of scattered\nstrong thunderstorms along with brief heavy rain. Flash flood \nwatch remain in effect for later today into Thursday for Pinal, \nGraham and Greenlee counties.\n\nDrier air moves in for Friday, though some lingering showers \npossible near the NM border, which could linger into the weekend as \nwell. \n\nTemperatures through Thursday will be at or slightly above normal,\nthen cooler than normal Friday into this weekend. Latest NBM \nhas a freeze potential at the highest elevations of the White \nMountains Sun/Mon morning.",
